content.text:
Yes—you were right. The recent design is:

- keep `provenance` only when generation actually cryptographically verifies it;
- stop treating `provenance_verified` as authoritative new state;
- let Packslip rely on its verified signed manifest/signer chain.

So #13105 should not synthesize `provenance` from Packslip links. The proper fix is to treat old Packslip provenance fields as legacy metadata and enforce Packslip’s signer ratchet instead. I’m revising the PR around that boundary and will explain the change publicly on the PR.

